.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAP-DELETE-NODE 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eap-delete-node \- remove a worker node's registration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eap delete-node
.BR \-\-node | \-n
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes a worker node's registration.
.PP
A node name belongs to the principal that first registered it: a worker
logged in as anybody else is refused that name, so that it cannot take
over another node's assignments and the application credentials that go
with them. Deleting the registration is how the name is freed, which is
why this action needs an administrator even though the other node
actions do not.
.PP
It does not stop the node. The instances assigned to it keep their
leases until those run out, and a worker that is still running finds
itself unregistered on its next renewal and registers again. To take a
node out of service, stop its
.B euclid-wrk
first; its leases then expire and its instances are placed elsewhere.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-node " " \fINAME\fR
Name of the node to delete. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The registration was removed.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the caller is not an authenticated
administrator, or no node of that name is registered.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
sudo systemctl stop euclid-wrk          # on the node
euclid-cli eap delete-node --node raspi-01
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eap (1),
.BR euclid-wrk (8),
.BR euclid-cli-eap-list-nodes (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eap-get-node (1)
